  "raw": "ima Vavi said the federation’s vision was that the workers would not form another federation or union, but trade unions with political agendas would first be removed from being registered as trade unions.\nVavi added that Cosatu would remain neutral and a strong commercial organisation meant taking sides was \"a mistake\".\nWe need our current approach which consists of neutralism …\nWhen you take your eyes off the ball and become what is called an ideological trade union, we are giving them a lot of powers. Therefore its very important for us to stay neutral.\nConrad Mofokeng of the South African National Civic Organisation (Sanco) supported Vavi and also questioned why Numsa was politicising Cosatu in light of its role as service union.\nI think two crucial points here are one – Nomsa is being used by some diaspora faction within Cosatu for their own purposes… Another issue is what it means when people point out other people make mistakes, how",
  "serialized": "ima Vavi said the federation’s vision was that the workers would not form another federation or union, but trade unions with political agendas would first be removed from being registered as trade unions. Vavi added that Cosatu would remain neutral and a strong commercial organisation meant taking sides was \"a mistake\". We need our current approach which consists of neutralism … When you take your eyes off the ball and become what is called an ideological trade union, we are giving them a lot of powers. Therefore its very important for us to stay neutral. Conrad Mofokeng of the South African National Civic Organisation (Sanco) supported Vavi and also questioned why Numsa was politicising Cosatu in light of its role as service union. I think two crucial points here are one – Nomsa is being used by some diaspora faction within Cosatu for their own purposes… Another issue is what it means when people point out other people make mistakes, how",
